  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>A dressed basalt slab a metre and a half high, set on edge as a wind screen and left standing when its hearth moved nightward. Screens are never taken along and never re-dressed, so the line of them running dayward from the present cluster is a physical count of generations. This one is the eleventh back and carries the polish that blown glass grit puts on anything which stands still, much heavier on the dayward face than on the other. It was recorded in place and not lifted, and the accession consists of a cast and a core.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
    }
  ],
